 {r}←{iniFile}(fns Run)y;⎕TRAP;testFlag;trapFlag;more;A;F;M;R;G;parms;buff;S;CaDir;congaFolder;congaName;congaWarning;⎕IO;⎕ML
⍝ Starts a Plodder server.
⍝ For special arrangements pass `fns` which might by just {1} in case you don't need to make any.
⍝ That function gets `G` passed as right argument and is expected to return 1 in case of success and 0 otherwise.
 ⎕TRAP←0 'S'
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 (testFlag trapFlag)←2↑y,(≢y)↓¯1 ¯1
 EnableCONTINUE_workspaces ⍬
 ExposeRootNameProperties ⍬
 G←⎕NS''
 G.AppName←'Plodder'            ⍝ Might get overwritten by INI file later on
 G←EstablishPlatformVars G
 CreateRefs ##
 F.PolishCurrentDir
 CheckForRide G                 ⍝ An early RIDE works only with command line parms
 iniFile←PolishInifilePath{0<⎕NC ⍵:⍎⍵ ⋄ 'server.ini'}'iniFile'
 G(ProcessIniFile)←iniFile
 R←CopyRumba ⍬                  ⍝ R points to Rumba[Lean].Core
 (congaFolder congaWarning)←CopyConga R.## G.INI
 congaName←'DEFAULT'G.INI.Get'Config' 'CongaName'
 {}R.InitConga congaFolder congaName
 G.INI CheckForRide G           ⍝ Again because now the INI might allow a Ride
 parms←CreateServerParms G
 :If (⊂testFlag)∊0 1
     G.TestFlag←testFlag        ⍝ Overwrite INI setting
 :Else
     G.TestFlag←0 G.INI.Get'CONFIG:TestFlag'
 :EndIf
 :If trapFlag∊0 1
     G.Trap←parms.Trap←trapFlag ⍝ Otherwise both keep what the INI file says: [TRAP]Policy and [TRAP]Rumba
 :EndIf

 parms←CheckServerParms parms
 ⍎parms.Context,'.G←G'          ⍝ Only now: CheckServerParms has made sure that `Context` exists
 G←OpenWindowsEventLog G
 WindowsEventLog'Starting'
 G←EstablishSecrets G
 #.⎕SHADOW'ErrorParms' ⋄ 'ErrorParms'#.⎕NS''
 #.ErrorParms←SetErrorParms ##.HandleError.CreateParms
 ⎕TRAP←G.Trap SetTrap G
 EstablishHandlersForRumbaEvents G
 parms.Folder←⊃G.INI.Get'Logging:Folder'
 'Problem with the folder holding the log file'Assert'CREATE!'F.CheckPath parms.Folder
 G←OpenAppLog G
 :If 0<≢congaWarning
 :AndIf 2=G.⎕NC'AppLogTie'
     AppLog'*** Warning: ',congaWarning
 :EndIf
 Assert fns G
 #.ErrorParms.off←0
 #.ErrorParms.killThreads←0
 #.ErrorParms.signal←689
 ⎕TRAP←(⊂#.ErrorParms.signal'C' '→∆Crashed'),⎕TRAP   ⍝ HandleError signals this once it has processed a
                                                     ⍝ crash. It must come first: the catch-all entry
                                                     ⍝ SetTrap installs would otherwise match it and loop

 :If G.INI.Get'CONFIG:Secure'
 :AndIf G.INI.Exist'CERTIFICATES' 'CA_Folder'
 :AndIf 0<≢CaDir←⊃G.INI.Get'CERTIFICATES' 'CA_Folder'
     {}##.RumbaLean.Core.DRC.SetProp'.' 'RootCertDir'CaDir
 :EndIf

 G.Server←r←parms R.Start congaFolder congaName ⍝ <=== Work horse

 DQ'.'
 ⎕DL 3
 OFF
 :Return

∆Crashed:                       ⍝ HandleError has saved and logged the crash and then signalled
 ⎕TRAP←0 'S'                    ⍝ Disarm first: a failure below must not re-enter here
 {}{0::0 ⋄ 'error'WindowsEventLog'Stopped due to a crash'}⍬
 {}{0::0 ⋄ AppLogError'Stopped due to a crash'}⍬
 :If IsConnectedToRide          ⍝ With a Ride attached we don't ⎕OFF, for obvious reasons
     ∘∘∘                        ⍝ Check it out, dear ⎕AN, in particular '∆' #.ErrorParms.⎕NL 2
 :EndIf
 ⎕OFF 125                       ⍝ Enforce a restart, as Rumba's ErrorInRumba does
⍝Done
